WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.350
Welcome to LeafLedger. This walkthrough uses real application screens and fictional

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.700
practice records for two made-up companies, Riverbend Tobacco Works and Harbor Leaf

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:16.437
Imports. Nothing here is a real business, and nothing you see is submitted to any agency.

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:22.174
LeafLedger runs on your own computer, and your records stay there. The overview shows the

00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:27.460
four steps of every month: complete setup, add the month's files, prepare, review.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:34.089
Setup is where you describe the business exactly as TTB and FDA know it. The practice

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:39.748
workspace is already filled in: the companies, each permit with its number, the product

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:45.536
classes each permit reports, and the products with their units. For your own business you

00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:50.740
enter this once. LeafLedger never fills in a fact it cannot verify; it asks you.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.128
Next, the source file layouts tell LeafLedger which column in your monthly export holds

00:00:57.128 --> 00:01:02.416
which fact. You can use the standard column names, or type the headings your own system

00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:07.826
produces. Below that, the account mapping links every value in your Account column to one

00:01:07.826 --> 00:01:13.054
reporting transaction type. An account that is not mapped stops the month. It is never

00:01:13.054 --> 00:01:13.540
guessed.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:20.612
Open Monthly cycle, type the reporting month, here August 2026, and click Load month. Each

00:01:20.612 --> 00:01:26.452
month has its own source files and its own results, and nothing from an earlier month is

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:27.580
ever overwritten.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:33.499
Add the month's export files. In the practice set, that is one file from the

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:38.889
manufacturer's records and one from the importer's, chosen with the matching profile.

00:01:38.889 --> 00:01:44.343
LeafLedger stores each file exactly as supplied and records its fingerprint, so a file

00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:47.260
that changes later can never be used silently.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:53.942
Click Prepare this month. LeafLedger reads every row, checks every captured regulation,

00:01:53.942 --> 00:01:59.395
and renders the draft forms. On the first month there is no earlier filing to compare

00:01:59.395 --> 00:02:04.720
against; from the second month on, last month's filing is selected automatically so

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.570
opening stock is checked against the previous closing stock.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:15.311
Each preparation is archived with a time stamp and a result. The practice month comes back

00:02:15.311 --> 00:02:20.827
as Review required. That is the normal outcome: the numbers reconcile, and LeafLedger is

00:02:20.827 --> 00:02:23.710
telling you what still needs a human decision.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:30.720
Review and export shows two things side by side. The engine status, Ready to file, means

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.697
every row reconciled with zero blocking exceptions. The open items below each say what to

00:02:36.697 --> 00:02:42.674
do: here, the official copies of the forms are not yet among the evidence, and the drafts

00:02:42.674 --> 00:02:48.718
are watermarked until the official rendering has been validated. LeafLedger flags; it does

00:02:48.718 --> 00:02:49.390
not guess.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:56.371
Further down are the draft forms, line by line. Line 7.d, the opening stock, is 100,000

00:02:56.371 --> 00:03:02.320
sticks, and beside it LeafLedger names the source rows that produced it. Every number on

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:08.403
every form traces back to your own records. Zero lines are folded away so you can read the

00:03:08.403 --> 00:03:09.620
lines that matter.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:16.959
Each form is also rendered as a PDF on the official template, watermarked as a draft, with

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:22.990
the certification left blank. You review it, you sign it, you file it. LeafLedger never

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.070
files anything on your behalf.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:31.854
History lists every preparation ever made. Corrections are recorded as new versions that

00:03:31.854 --> 00:03:37.537
supersede the old ones; nothing is deleted, so you can always show what you prepared and

00:03:37.537 --> 00:03:37.860
when.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:45.044
Finally, create an encrypted backup with a passphrase you choose. The passphrase is never

00:03:45.044 --> 00:03:51.059
stored, so keep it safe. That is the whole routine: setup once, then every month add the

00:03:51.059 --> 00:03:54.340
files, prepare, and review. Thanks for watching.
